WEBVTT

00:09.050 --> 00:11.469
EMERGENCY MEDICAL CENTER

00:18.977 --> 00:20.228
I need painkillers.

00:20.311 --> 00:23.231
- Please help my mom.
- We'll get to her soon.

00:23.314 --> 00:24.733
Are you sure?

00:24.816 --> 00:25.650
Come in.

00:25.734 --> 00:28.028
- She can't move her face.
- Just wait.

00:28.111 --> 00:30.655
- Can someone help her?
- We'll get to her soon.

00:31.781 --> 00:33.658
Coming through.

00:33.742 --> 00:34.784
Coming through here.

00:36.494 --> 00:37.495
KANGBUK SAMSUNG HOSPITAL

00:37.579 --> 00:38.872
Doctor, please…

00:39.414 --> 00:40.749
Out of the way!

00:40.832 --> 00:43.001
Out of the way! He's crashing here!

00:43.084 --> 00:45.712
- Stay with me.
- Open your eyes!

00:45.795 --> 00:46.796
Come on!

01:10.278 --> 01:11.279
- Thank you.
- Sure.

01:12.072 --> 01:14.199
What's your blood type?

01:16.785 --> 01:18.578
Blood pressure 80/50.

01:19.079 --> 01:20.330
Mom.

01:29.380 --> 01:30.423
Oh…

01:35.929 --> 01:38.431
- I'm sorry.
- No, no.

01:38.932 --> 01:39.766
You're fine.

01:45.814 --> 01:46.815
Let's go.

02:27.397 --> 02:30.775
BLOODHOUNDS

02:30.859 --> 02:32.110
KANGBUK SAMSUNG HOSPITAL

02:32.193 --> 02:34.154
- Mr. An Mun-ju?
- Yes.

02:40.201 --> 02:42.620
You're lucky
there wasn't any nerve damage.

02:43.621 --> 02:45.874
We can help with the scar, you know?

02:45.957 --> 02:48.001
Now that the would is all sealed up,

02:48.751 --> 02:51.921
we can do a procedure
that will keep it from scarring too badly.

02:52.547 --> 02:53.631
Will it be expensive?

02:53.715 --> 02:55.466
It can be pricey, yes.

02:56.426 --> 02:59.679
Let me show you a photo
of a recent procedure.

03:00.722 --> 03:03.016
- See the scar there?
- Yeah.

03:03.099 --> 03:05.059
This is the before photo.

03:05.143 --> 03:08.438
- And this is after the laser treatment.
- Oh.

03:08.521 --> 03:10.815
It's your face. You're young.

03:10.899 --> 03:13.610
It would be wise to look into it,
in my opinion.

03:15.486 --> 03:17.655
It's okay. I'll be fine.
Thank you so much.

03:19.574 --> 03:21.618
Mr. Choi Han-seon?

03:22.535 --> 03:23.620
Come on in.

03:23.703 --> 03:24.662
Hey.

03:28.875 --> 03:29.709
You okay?

03:31.336 --> 03:33.546
- Show me.
- No.

03:33.630 --> 03:34.631
Show me.

03:42.138 --> 03:43.389
Oh God.

03:47.227 --> 03:48.311
How many stitches?

03:49.229 --> 03:50.188
Thirty.

03:50.271 --> 03:53.733
Those motherfuckers.
How do we get back at them?

03:56.236 --> 03:57.070
The cops?

03:59.530 --> 04:03.451
Call the cops,
and your mom's dead.

04:08.206 --> 04:10.124
- We can't.
- Why's that?

04:10.208 --> 04:11.709
He said they'll kill my mom.

04:13.461 --> 04:15.213
Shit.

04:16.005 --> 04:17.590
Wait, the contract.

04:19.259 --> 04:20.093
Right.

04:20.635 --> 04:21.552
Here.

04:22.262 --> 04:24.264
There's a "loan extension fee" in it.

04:25.223 --> 04:28.810
You have to pay 10% of the principal
every single week.

04:29.644 --> 04:31.854
Your mom took fifty million,
so the fee is five.

04:33.106 --> 04:35.400
But if you miss a payment,
the fee doubles,

04:35.483 --> 04:37.860
and the interest jumps to 20%.

04:37.944 --> 04:40.405
Assholes wrote it in fine print
so no one sees it.

04:41.281 --> 04:43.408
It's a con. Your mom didn't know.

04:44.117 --> 04:45.118
What do I do?

04:45.201 --> 04:46.786
You have to pay it all back.

04:47.578 --> 04:49.455
She used your home as collateral.

04:50.081 --> 04:52.208
We're fucked.

04:53.584 --> 04:55.670
Damn it.

05:03.261 --> 05:06.222
Let's go eat. On me, What do you want?

05:09.475 --> 05:10.435
Rib eye.

05:11.311 --> 05:12.687
Oh, come on.

05:12.770 --> 05:13.730
Are you joking?

05:14.522 --> 05:15.815
No, I want rib eye.

05:17.191 --> 05:18.067
All right.

05:19.402 --> 05:21.779
Spicy stir-fried pork
is as good as rib eye.

05:24.073 --> 05:24.949
I'll take it.

05:27.076 --> 05:28.828
I always come here after a workout.

05:28.911 --> 05:31.998
It's my routine. Kinda perfect,
so don't ruin it for me, okay?

05:32.081 --> 05:33.374
Just be quiet and eat your food.

05:33.458 --> 05:35.084
- Understood?
- Understood.

05:35.168 --> 05:37.128
- There she is!
- Hello.

05:37.211 --> 05:39.255
Hello. Hi.

05:39.339 --> 05:40.340
How are you, dear?

05:40.423 --> 05:42.050
- Two spicy porks, please.
- Oh, of course.

05:42.133 --> 05:43.468
And you brought a friend with you.

05:43.551 --> 05:45.136
- Hello.
- He boxes with me.

05:45.219 --> 05:46.220
That's great.

05:51.309 --> 05:53.019
I need to take this.

05:53.102 --> 05:53.936
Okay.

05:54.687 --> 05:57.357
Hey, hey. Yeah, this is Woo-jin

05:57.857 --> 05:58.733
How are you?

05:59.942 --> 06:01.527
Uh, well, the thing is…

06:08.409 --> 06:09.994
MY SON

06:11.496 --> 06:12.538
Hi, Gun-woo.

06:13.122 --> 06:14.957
Hey, mom. Woo-jin looked at the contract.

06:15.041 --> 06:16.793
Apparently, these guys are con men.

06:16.876 --> 06:18.044
They tricked you into signing.

06:18.795 --> 06:20.088
None of it's your fault, Mom.

06:20.171 --> 06:21.422
Thank you, son.

06:23.341 --> 06:26.010
What did they…
What did they say about your face?

06:26.761 --> 06:28.471
Hm. They said it will be fine.

06:28.971 --> 06:30.390
Oh, thank goodness.

06:31.599 --> 06:33.559
And I'll clean up everything with Woo-jin.

06:33.643 --> 06:35.144
You should stay home and rest, okay?

06:37.063 --> 06:40.650
No, no, no. Don't do anything.
I'll go clean up.

06:40.733 --> 06:43.694
It's fine. I'll do it
on my way back home, hm?

06:43.778 --> 06:45.279
Your food is ready.

06:49.200 --> 06:51.869
Mom, I'll have to call you back
in a little bit, okay?

06:51.953 --> 06:53.704
- Oh, all right.
- Mm-hm.

07:00.128 --> 07:03.005
Come on.
Just help me out this one time.

07:03.089 --> 07:04.882
It's not for me. It's for a friend.

07:05.883 --> 07:08.970
You know I'll pay it all back on time.
There won't be an issue.

07:10.263 --> 07:12.765
Jesus, we can get a second-tier loan
from anywhere.

07:13.933 --> 07:15.601
Please give me a first-tier loan.

07:15.685 --> 07:17.979
I am seriously, seriously begging you.

07:18.563 --> 07:20.523
Because I care about this kid, man.

07:22.400 --> 07:25.319
Remember how many loan payments
I collected for you back in the day?

07:26.362 --> 07:28.322
You owe me, man. Come on.

07:58.060 --> 08:00.021
Whoa, you should have got me.

08:00.605 --> 08:02.982
- It just came out.
- Dig in.

08:03.649 --> 08:06.110
- The best spicy pork in all of Korea.
- Oh.

08:12.992 --> 08:14.660
- Right? Let's eat.
- Mm.

08:26.214 --> 08:28.966
LET'S TALK AT THE OFFICE

08:29.550 --> 08:31.177
He has a quick temper.

08:31.260 --> 08:32.553
Keep your head down.

08:32.637 --> 08:34.263
- I'll do the talking.
- Okay.

08:37.808 --> 08:39.602
- Mr. Seo.
- Yes?

08:39.685 --> 08:40.853
How much is this?

08:41.729 --> 08:43.439
It's worth 20 million.

08:43.523 --> 08:45.733
Come on, bro. Woo-jin is here.

08:47.443 --> 08:49.111
You got some nerve dropping off the grid,

08:49.195 --> 08:52.114
then coming here to ask me for money, huh?

08:52.198 --> 08:54.617
Come on,
what do you have to say to me, huh?

08:55.117 --> 08:58.079
- I'm… sorry, okay? You look good.
- Let go of me.

08:58.162 --> 09:00.915
You little shit.

09:00.998 --> 09:02.375
- Sit.
- Hey, sit.

09:02.458 --> 09:03.292
Okay.

09:08.464 --> 09:09.298
All right.

09:10.216 --> 09:11.592
So how'd you get in debt?

09:11.676 --> 09:14.679
Some thugs got him. Smile Capital.

09:15.263 --> 09:18.099
Smile Capital? In Gwangan-dong?

09:18.724 --> 09:20.142
I'm not really sure.

09:20.935 --> 09:22.270
Oh shit.

09:23.187 --> 09:26.065
Yeah, Smile Capital isn't just
a bunch of goons.

09:26.148 --> 09:27.316
They're a huge company.

09:28.150 --> 09:29.402
How much was it?

09:29.986 --> 09:30.861
A hundred.

09:35.950 --> 09:37.118
You're screwed, huh?

09:37.994 --> 09:40.621
Yeah, exactly, so help him out, man.
You got enough money.

09:44.208 --> 09:46.794
Here's a first-tier loan
of 100 million.

09:49.547 --> 09:51.132
Wow! Thanks so much.

09:53.676 --> 09:55.678
In exchange, you'll do some work for me.

09:56.971 --> 09:58.889
Thanks to COVID, business is booming.

09:58.973 --> 10:01.225
Let's strike while the iron's hot
and make some real money.

10:02.018 --> 10:03.102
Just help me out,

10:03.185 --> 10:06.522
and I'll throw in a bonus
for each collection.

10:07.607 --> 10:10.484
Uh… I don't know.

10:10.568 --> 10:11.694
Jesus.

10:11.777 --> 10:13.738
Just work as a bloodhound for one year.

10:15.114 --> 10:17.074
Listen, this is a real opportunity.

10:17.575 --> 10:19.452
You two can make some big money here.

10:20.369 --> 10:22.913
What other options do you have
to make this much?

10:22.997 --> 10:24.582
I know you're right.

10:24.665 --> 10:26.626
- Come on.
- It's just a bit unexpected.

10:27.668 --> 10:30.087
- Come on, give me an answer.
- Hey, we should go.

10:31.255 --> 10:32.089
Huh?

10:32.173 --> 10:34.425
Don't these runs involve
beating people up?

10:36.469 --> 10:38.888
If you prey on the weak for money,
you're a thug.

10:40.473 --> 10:41.390
We're boxers.

10:44.018 --> 10:44.935
Okay, listen here.

10:45.686 --> 10:48.648
Smile Capital will kill you
if you don't pay them back.

10:48.731 --> 10:50.316
They're gonna sell your organs.

11:02.662 --> 11:03.621
The hell?

11:03.704 --> 11:06.540
Bro, thanks so much, but we can't.

11:08.250 --> 11:09.835
Come on, let's go. Yeah, go on.

11:10.419 --> 11:11.545
What are you trying to do here?

11:14.048 --> 11:15.257
Let go of me.

11:24.767 --> 11:26.060
I'm just kidding.

11:27.561 --> 11:28.729
See ya.

11:31.565 --> 11:32.525
Hey, let's go.

11:36.696 --> 11:37.947
Goddammit!

11:39.407 --> 11:40.408
Hey, boxer.

11:47.081 --> 11:48.916
- Stamp it.
- Okay.

11:50.209 --> 11:52.670
Once your business takes off,
give us a cut, okay?

11:52.753 --> 11:56.173
Oh, thank you. Thank you so much.

12:01.512 --> 12:02.972
- Great work.
- Let's go.

13:11.415 --> 13:12.666
You're late.

13:13.501 --> 13:14.668
Sorry about that.

13:15.169 --> 13:17.379
Here. It's all in there.

13:17.463 --> 13:19.632
This is all the money we collected today.

13:21.008 --> 13:23.511
We've been collecting IDs
from homeless people

13:23.594 --> 13:24.512
to take out the loans.

13:25.721 --> 13:27.223
Who are you?

13:27.306 --> 13:29.475
No one. Keep working.

13:29.558 --> 13:30.476
Okay.

13:31.936 --> 13:33.687
We're working as fast as we can

13:33.771 --> 13:35.189
to get you the amount you need.

13:39.735 --> 13:41.278
When can you get it done?

13:41.362 --> 13:43.364
This week? I'll try, sir.

13:43.447 --> 13:46.116
KIM JUN-MIN

13:49.912 --> 13:51.705
MASKS ARE REQUIRED
IN THE WAITING ROOM

13:56.669 --> 13:59.755
Hello, I hope I didn't keep you waiting
too long.

13:59.839 --> 14:02.633
DREAM ON CAPITAL

14:02.716 --> 14:04.635
Oh, why aren't you wearing your mask?

14:05.553 --> 14:06.387
I'll put it back on.

14:06.470 --> 14:07.680
There's no need.

14:07.763 --> 14:09.682
I asked you why you took it off.
Answer me.

14:10.266 --> 14:12.309
I mean,
you kept us waiting for 30 minutes.

14:12.393 --> 14:13.561
It was getting stuffy in here.

14:13.644 --> 14:16.272
Whoa! How do you think
you're gonna protect people

14:16.355 --> 14:17.565
if you don't have any patience?

14:17.648 --> 14:20.442
Jeez, man. What does that even have to do
with me wearing a mask?

14:20.526 --> 14:21.777
Get out.

14:22.987 --> 14:23.821
Get out now!

14:24.780 --> 14:27.199
Oh, fuck.

14:29.451 --> 14:31.078
Little shit.

14:32.705 --> 14:34.290
Jeez.

14:35.833 --> 14:38.043
- You took your mask off too.
- Uh, no.

14:38.127 --> 14:38.961
You did. I saw it.

14:39.545 --> 14:40.838
I had it pulled down.

14:40.921 --> 14:43.340
If you pulled it down,
then you took it off, you idiot.

14:43.424 --> 14:44.258
Get out.

14:45.134 --> 14:46.176
Get the fuck out!

14:46.927 --> 14:47.970
Ah, damn it.

14:49.346 --> 14:51.348
"Oh no. Damn it."

14:51.849 --> 14:53.934
"Oh no! Damn it!"

14:54.018 --> 14:55.394
Idiots.

14:58.731 --> 15:00.107
Pull it down. Let's see it.

15:03.903 --> 15:05.154
So what's your name, son?

15:05.779 --> 15:06.822
Cheon Dong-woo, sir.

15:06.906 --> 15:08.240
Hm. Height?

15:08.324 --> 15:10.284
I'm 187 centimeters tall, sir.

15:10.951 --> 15:11.911
Any training or…?

15:11.994 --> 15:14.330
I've trained in kickboxing and hapkido
for ten years, sir.

15:14.413 --> 15:17.541
- Your major?
- I majored in Security Services.

15:20.336 --> 15:23.297
Oh! A man's man. Look at you!

15:23.380 --> 15:24.340
Military?

15:24.423 --> 15:25.341
I was exempted.

15:26.508 --> 15:28.093
Tore my ACL playing volleyball.

15:29.470 --> 15:30.304
Oh.

15:32.181 --> 15:34.808
- Never mind. See you next time.
- Why are you turning me down, sir?

15:35.559 --> 15:38.270
- I need a marine, kid. Get out of here.
- Does it really have to be?

15:38.354 --> 15:40.189
Uh-huh. Mm-hm.

15:41.106 --> 15:43.776
Well, shit, you should have mentioned that
in the job posting.

15:44.318 --> 15:46.403
Oh, really? And why is that?

15:46.487 --> 15:47.905
Because you wasted my time!

15:48.489 --> 15:51.033
Who the fuck do you think
you're talking to like that?

15:51.116 --> 15:52.326
Elder, my ass.

15:52.409 --> 15:54.662
You don't screw around with people
like that.

15:58.374 --> 16:00.209
I'll see you next time, uh-huh?

16:00.793 --> 16:01.627
Yeah.

16:04.171 --> 16:07.091
MARINE
IF IT DOESN'T WORK, MAKE IT WORK!

16:11.261 --> 16:13.180
1216TH CLASS HONG WOO-JIN

16:23.357 --> 16:24.316
It's you.

16:25.776 --> 16:28.570
- Why are we running?
- He's a higher rank!

16:31.907 --> 16:36.370
There's only one man in all of Korea
who can move a trillion in cash

16:36.453 --> 16:37.621
- with just a phone call.
- Whoa!

16:38.372 --> 16:39.581
Bang Seong-ho that is.

16:39.665 --> 16:40.541
Oh.

16:41.375 --> 16:45.045
And only one single person knows
what Chairman Bang even looks like.

16:45.129 --> 16:46.839
Literally only one person?

16:46.922 --> 16:48.465
Yeah, but keep it quiet, son.

16:49.466 --> 16:52.553
Now, Chairman Bang trusted only one man
in his life,

16:52.636 --> 16:54.138
and that is Mr. Choi.

16:54.221 --> 16:58.642
Mr. Choi is the reason I can actually
make a living doing all of this here.

16:58.726 --> 17:01.145
You understand this whole ecosystem now?

17:01.228 --> 17:02.271
- Yes.
- Yeah.

17:02.354 --> 17:04.565
Ah, all right. Yeah.

17:05.065 --> 17:07.192
Mr. Choi is now looking to hire someone.

17:07.901 --> 17:09.570
Someone smart and fearless

17:09.653 --> 17:11.864
who is willing to put themself
in harm's way.

17:11.947 --> 17:13.240
Someone with a heart of pure gold

17:13.323 --> 17:17.327
who also has some knowledge
about our unique… line of work.

17:17.411 --> 17:21.123
I've been seeing dozens of applicants
all day, but honestly,

17:21.749 --> 17:24.793
they just keep… falling short.

17:24.877 --> 17:27.713
But then my junior marine gave me a call!

17:27.796 --> 17:29.757
Impeccable timing, I will say, huh!

17:29.840 --> 17:31.050
Oh man!

17:31.133 --> 17:33.719
And my friend's a marine. Senior marine.

17:34.303 --> 17:35.179
What class, man?

17:35.262 --> 17:36.764
The 1207th, sir.

17:36.847 --> 17:40.225
I'm the 734th.

17:40.309 --> 17:43.479
- Huh?
- Oh, I like this, man.

17:43.562 --> 17:46.648
Mr. Choi is gonna love you two fellas.
I'll put in a good word for you.

17:47.483 --> 17:48.984
Now I just need your IDs.

17:49.735 --> 17:50.569
Uh, sir.

17:52.029 --> 17:55.741
I called
because I need to help him get a loan.

17:56.366 --> 17:59.578
That's why I'm telling you
to go meet with Mr. Choi, son.

17:59.661 --> 18:01.747
He's a wild tiger on the outside,

18:01.830 --> 18:04.833
but he has the deepest,
most understanding heart. I swear.

18:04.917 --> 18:06.877
He's a true marine

18:06.960 --> 18:09.338
who takes care of you
once he accepts you as one of his own.

18:10.047 --> 18:11.381
He's our senior?

18:12.758 --> 18:14.384
Is Mr. Choi a marine? I don't know.

18:14.468 --> 18:15.552
Is he?

18:17.429 --> 18:20.182
I think he got an exemption
for dropping out of school too early.

18:21.558 --> 18:24.311
Oh, so it was a figure of speech

18:24.394 --> 18:26.605
like how rappers say
everything is hip-hop?

18:26.688 --> 18:27.564
Am I right?

18:30.609 --> 18:34.238
What the hell are you talking about?
Just write down your goddamn IDs.

18:34.738 --> 18:35.572
Yep.

18:42.329 --> 18:44.289
- Judging by his face…
- Yeah?

18:44.373 --> 18:45.541
I think this will work.

18:46.250 --> 18:49.378
- Thanks, brother.
- Yeah. No need to thank me, all right?

18:50.379 --> 18:52.214
How many of them did you fight?

18:53.590 --> 18:55.134
- Maybe ten?
- Oh.

18:55.634 --> 18:58.345
- One guy got me.
- Just one?

18:58.846 --> 19:00.139
He was built like a tank.

19:00.806 --> 19:01.682
He headbutted me.

19:02.307 --> 19:04.643
Hard to block a headbutt.

19:07.020 --> 19:11.525
So, what if they… offer you work
as a debt collector

19:12.109 --> 19:13.527
to pay off your mom's loans?

19:20.075 --> 19:21.285
We'll figure it out.

19:34.798 --> 19:36.508
Excellent work, as usual.

19:36.592 --> 19:37.926
Okay, that's fine.

19:38.427 --> 19:41.471
No, no, no, no.
Don't worry, we'll take care of it.

19:41.555 --> 19:43.557
That happened to be Mr. Oh's specialty.

19:44.308 --> 19:45.434
Mm-hm.

19:46.018 --> 19:48.896
I think we should all go
to Yang-jung's place.

19:49.396 --> 19:50.230
All right.

19:53.317 --> 19:55.569
Yang Jae-myeong went around
taking out loans

19:55.652 --> 19:57.154
from seven different loan sharks today.

19:57.237 --> 19:59.615
It turned out to be 400 million in cash.

20:00.282 --> 20:03.535
Then he delivered it to a man
that works at Smile Capital.

20:04.953 --> 20:05.913
Know him?

20:07.581 --> 20:08.957
No, I don't.

20:09.041 --> 20:13.003
Yang Jae-myeong is stealing homeless IDs
to create shell companies.

20:13.587 --> 20:15.589
He then uses those IDs
to borrow a lot of money.

20:16.381 --> 20:18.258
The loan sharks don't manage to catch on

20:18.342 --> 20:20.636
because they never share information
with each other.

20:20.719 --> 20:21.553
And then…

20:22.137 --> 20:25.307
Then they try to collect all the money
from a fake company.

20:25.891 --> 20:29.561
This was plotted by someone
who knows very well how cash flows.

20:29.645 --> 20:32.856
Looks like Yang Jae-myeong
is just a pawn here really.

20:33.774 --> 20:35.400
So how do you know all this?

20:35.984 --> 20:38.403
Well, what year was it? 2000?

20:39.029 --> 20:44.076
A volunteer at an assisted living facility
stole a bunch of the patients' IDs.

20:44.576 --> 20:47.371
He then created
a bunch of shell companies with them,

20:47.454 --> 20:52.167
used those to take out
seven billion won worth of loans,

20:52.251 --> 20:53.961
then ran off to the Philippines.

20:54.461 --> 20:56.129
That's be ten billion today.

20:57.756 --> 20:58.632
What do we do?

20:59.258 --> 21:00.425
Huh?

21:00.509 --> 21:03.178
Those loan sharks are getting conned.

21:03.262 --> 21:04.972
They're kind of your colleagues.

21:05.055 --> 21:06.890
I'm sure they'll be able to figure it out.

21:07.599 --> 21:10.227
They can't exactly go to the cops,
can they?

21:11.144 --> 21:15.190
Hyeon-ju, this is something
they will really have to solve themselves.

21:16.525 --> 21:19.486
Listen, I'm done with that world.

21:20.237 --> 21:21.613
And I want to keep it that way.

21:21.697 --> 21:22.656
Sure.

21:23.156 --> 21:26.368
So, uh, so what ended up happening
to the guy in the Philippines.

21:26.451 --> 21:27.286
He got caught?

21:27.369 --> 21:30.205
The loan sharks
gathered up some bloodhounds

21:30.289 --> 21:32.165
and sent them to chase the guy down.

21:32.791 --> 21:33.625
Did he die?

21:36.962 --> 21:39.089
Man, that's awful.

21:39.840 --> 21:41.633
Hyeon-ju, what would you think

21:41.717 --> 21:43.552
if I hired someone to help you
with your work?

21:44.136 --> 21:45.637
No.

21:45.721 --> 21:48.515
I mean, it's dangerous out there.
Look, you got hurt here.

21:48.598 --> 21:51.351
- It was just a scratch.
- Listen to me.

21:51.435 --> 21:53.937
Oh, no. No, no, no. I work better alone.

21:54.021 --> 21:55.105
Good night.

21:56.940 --> 21:57.858
You're a brat!

22:01.153 --> 22:02.112
Nice shot!

22:02.696 --> 22:03.530
So, uh…

22:04.239 --> 22:07.284
Sir, why did mess up that kid's face?

22:14.499 --> 22:15.542
Who told you?

22:15.625 --> 22:17.669
In-beom told me about it.

22:18.462 --> 22:19.880
He talks about these things?

22:20.756 --> 22:22.799
- It's just me, sir.
- Oh, I see.

22:27.304 --> 22:28.930
- Oh, nice.
- Good shot.

22:32.559 --> 22:35.145
That kid spat on my face
in front of the boys.

22:37.022 --> 22:38.523
I made an example out of him.

22:40.067 --> 22:41.985
You shouldn't get personally involved.

22:47.240 --> 22:48.200
Jang-do.

22:49.284 --> 22:53.538
Your men will never fear you
unless you have the balls to act.

22:54.706 --> 22:55.540
Yes sir.

22:57.626 --> 22:59.920
Why hasn't this rich kid contacted me?

23:00.003 --> 23:01.380
It's been a week.

23:01.880 --> 23:04.341
I'll have Mr. Park set up a meeting
for you.

23:04.424 --> 23:05.675
Don't worry. We'll win him over.

23:06.385 --> 23:07.219
All right.

23:25.153 --> 23:26.488
38TH NATIONAL ROOKIE APPLICATION

23:28.782 --> 23:31.284
Oh man, this kid is really athletic, huh?

23:31.910 --> 23:34.788
Didn't you use to box
back in the day too, sir?

23:34.871 --> 23:37.207
I was just an amateur.

23:37.916 --> 23:41.002
This body speaks to his diligence
and spirit.

23:41.086 --> 23:43.338
Bodies, they don't lie, you know?

23:43.922 --> 23:45.173
That's true, sir.

23:45.257 --> 23:49.344
But then he doesn't know anything
about the loan business, right?

23:51.888 --> 23:52.889
Oh, yeah.

23:52.973 --> 23:54.975
This is the kid hanging with Kim Gun-woo.

23:56.143 --> 23:58.145
According to the PI…

23:58.979 --> 24:01.440
…he beat up a bunch of gang members,

24:01.523 --> 24:03.650
then joined the Marines to hide from them.

24:04.192 --> 24:05.819
Since then, he's lived clean.

24:05.902 --> 24:09.531
He's been on some runs,
so he should know the basics.

24:10.740 --> 24:13.618
I think we should bring
the both of them in.

24:16.163 --> 24:18.707
- For the time being, let's meet Gun-woo.
- Sure.

24:19.499 --> 24:20.500
Right there.

24:24.212 --> 24:26.089
SUSHI

24:31.761 --> 24:32.971
- Hello, sir.
- Hello.

24:34.514 --> 24:36.349
You were introduced
through Mr. Moon, right?

24:36.433 --> 24:37.392
Yeah.

24:39.394 --> 24:40.437
This way, please.

24:47.068 --> 24:48.361
- Go ahead.
- Hm?

24:48.862 --> 24:49.821
- Yes.
- Oh.

25:28.735 --> 25:30.654
Hello, sir. I am Kim Gun-woo, sir.

25:30.737 --> 25:32.822
Oh. Sit down.

25:32.906 --> 25:33.740
Thanks.

25:42.666 --> 25:44.793
Don't worry.
You don't need to be formal with me.

25:44.876 --> 25:46.044
Yes, sir.

25:52.634 --> 25:54.386
Looks like you've been cut.

25:54.970 --> 25:56.805
Oh, yes sir, I have.

25:56.888 --> 25:59.391
I had to fight some loan sharks
who smashed up my mother's café.

26:02.352 --> 26:04.354
I used to be a loan shark myself.

26:06.439 --> 26:08.942
I've been retired a while.

26:09.526 --> 26:10.402
Yeah.

26:10.485 --> 26:13.029
Now, I'm dedicated
to offer zero-interests loans

26:13.113 --> 26:14.072
to sick people

26:15.198 --> 26:17.450
who can't afford to pay
for the treatments they need.

26:18.034 --> 26:18.868
Okay.

26:21.830 --> 26:23.498
I think I may have a job for you.

26:25.375 --> 26:28.336
There's a young girl
who has learning the business from me.

26:29.004 --> 26:30.088
Ah.

26:30.171 --> 26:31.965
We're actually not related.

26:33.466 --> 26:35.135
But she's the only family I have.

26:35.719 --> 26:36.761
Yeah.

26:36.845 --> 26:40.640
I worry a lot she may get herself hurt
while going around alone.

26:41.933 --> 26:43.727
I was hoping to hire a good person

26:43.810 --> 26:46.354
to stay by her side
and keep her safe, you know?

26:46.980 --> 26:48.148
Oh.

26:48.648 --> 26:50.317
So it won't involve any debt collection?

26:50.400 --> 26:52.944
No. No, no. No debt collection.

26:54.404 --> 26:56.823
- Just security.
- Oh.

26:56.906 --> 26:57.741
Yeah.

27:00.285 --> 27:03.079
I'm sorry,
you might find this a little rude,

27:03.830 --> 27:06.207
but I did some digging into your past.

27:06.291 --> 27:08.043
Oh, that's not a problem at all, sir.

27:08.126 --> 27:11.463
I learned that even though
you went through so many hardships,

27:12.589 --> 27:14.549
you've kept your heart and focus.

27:14.633 --> 27:18.762
You have a strong gaze
which makes me feel I can trust you.

27:21.222 --> 27:23.016
I can, am I right?

27:23.099 --> 27:24.059
Thank you, sir.

27:29.397 --> 27:30.231
Uh…

27:32.776 --> 27:34.277
Why did you start boxing?

27:34.361 --> 27:36.488
When I was little,
I wanted to get stronger.

27:37.072 --> 27:37.906
Why?

27:38.782 --> 27:41.618
Well, sir, my dad had never really been
much of a heavy drinker.

27:42.494 --> 27:45.038
Things got rough for us
in my first year of middle school.

27:45.121 --> 27:47.582
He started drinking
and hitting my mother when he was drunk.

27:48.166 --> 27:51.002
I wanted to stop him,
but I was too weak at the time.

27:54.130 --> 27:56.383
- They still together?
- Oh, no. Th--

27:57.050 --> 27:59.052
They got divorced
in my third year of middle school,

27:59.135 --> 28:00.428
and I haven't seen him since.

28:01.721 --> 28:04.057
- I grew up in the countryside.
- I see.

28:04.140 --> 28:07.435
And my father was a tenant farmer.

28:07.519 --> 28:08.395
Okay.

28:09.145 --> 28:10.230
I can still remember it.

28:11.147 --> 28:13.233
Ah, I think I was maybe ten.

28:14.067 --> 28:17.028
There was a blight on all our crops,

28:17.112 --> 28:19.030
and when we couldn't pay our rent,

28:19.823 --> 28:21.991
the landlord sent a group of his men

28:23.076 --> 28:24.953
to brutally beat my father…

28:27.455 --> 28:29.624
in front of everyone in the village.

28:30.208 --> 28:31.042
Mm-hm.

28:31.543 --> 28:33.461
My father was badly injured,

28:34.129 --> 28:36.423
but we couldn't afford
to go to the hospital,

28:38.299 --> 28:40.468
so we watched him die at home.

28:41.219 --> 28:44.389
That is why I became determined
to make money

28:45.223 --> 28:47.642
and do my best
to help all the people that…

28:49.644 --> 28:51.604
…can't afford medical treatment.

28:58.778 --> 29:02.907
Ah. Sorry,
that was a pretty lousy pep talk.

29:02.991 --> 29:06.411
What I was saying is that in the end,
we both came out of it with good hearts.

29:06.494 --> 29:09.873
Yeah. I've always tried to lead life
with my heart, sir.

29:16.129 --> 29:17.338
You don't talk much.

29:17.422 --> 29:20.842
Uh, yeah. Sorry, sir.
I've never been very good with words.

29:21.468 --> 29:23.094
- Oh, I see.
- Yeah.

29:28.141 --> 29:29.642
- Hey, over here.
- Okay.

29:31.352 --> 29:32.187
How did it go?

29:33.646 --> 29:35.106
It went well, I think.

29:35.190 --> 29:37.942
He basically spoke the whole time.
I just sat there and listened to him.

29:38.026 --> 29:40.570
Hell yeah!
I told you things would go well.

29:42.280 --> 29:44.365
Hey.

29:44.449 --> 29:45.700
So how was he?

29:46.409 --> 29:48.661
Well, the kid is certainly no fun.

29:51.414 --> 29:52.624
But he's good.

29:54.876 --> 29:55.710
Good.

29:59.631 --> 30:01.090
Watch it.

30:03.384 --> 30:06.721
He needs money as soon as possible.
Take care of it by the end of the day.

30:06.805 --> 30:07.639
Yes, sir.

30:08.932 --> 30:10.725
- Just give me a little.
- No, eat up.

30:11.267 --> 30:12.477
It's a bit…

30:14.979 --> 30:17.232
Ah!

30:17.315 --> 30:19.234
I hope this okay for you, dear.

30:19.317 --> 30:23.071
Ma'am, I love kimchi jjigae.

30:23.154 --> 30:24.781
- May I try--
- Oh, yeah.

30:27.075 --> 30:28.910
Careful. It's hot.

30:28.993 --> 30:31.204
So good! Thank you so much.

30:31.287 --> 30:32.789
Please enjoy it. My pleasure.

30:34.123 --> 30:39.045
We really appreciate your help
with what we're going through.

30:39.128 --> 30:42.048
Oh, it's nothing.
Besides, he's a good friend.

30:43.591 --> 30:44.968
And marine, "Ack!"

30:45.677 --> 30:47.929
Things are gonna work out.

30:48.721 --> 30:49.848
Thank you.

30:49.931 --> 30:51.349
Now dig in there, boys.

30:51.432 --> 30:53.101
- Yes, ma'am!
- Thanks for cooking.

30:53.184 --> 30:54.018
Of course.

30:56.271 --> 30:57.105
Huh?

30:58.356 --> 30:59.816
- I'll go.
- Okay.

31:00.316 --> 31:01.401
Who is it?

31:04.487 --> 31:05.530
Uh, hello?

31:06.239 --> 31:08.116
Good evening. I work for Mr. Choi.

31:08.867 --> 31:09.784
Oh.

31:13.496 --> 31:14.497
Um, hello.

31:14.581 --> 31:16.791
Here, a hundred million.

31:17.375 --> 31:18.376
What?

31:18.459 --> 31:20.503
This is an advance
on two years' worth of your pay.

31:21.921 --> 31:23.464
I mean…

31:31.055 --> 31:32.974
Work starts at ten tomorrow.

31:33.057 --> 31:35.685
I will text you with the address.

31:40.398 --> 31:41.399
Thank you, sir.

31:42.358 --> 31:43.985
Thank you so, so much.

31:44.569 --> 31:46.905
Well, you should be thanking Mr. Choi.

31:46.988 --> 31:48.239
- Yeah.
- Good night.

31:49.782 --> 31:50.700
Thank you.

32:17.685 --> 32:20.021
These are so good.

32:20.104 --> 32:21.481
Next time, I'll make you more.

32:24.150 --> 32:25.151
Who was it?

32:27.904 --> 32:29.405
It, um…

32:31.866 --> 32:36.704
Uh, Mom, so I… I managed to get some work
through a friend of Woo-jin.

32:37.580 --> 32:38.456
What kind?

32:39.040 --> 32:43.169
I'll start working as a bodyguard
for a rich businessman's family member.

32:44.504 --> 32:46.005
Apparently he liked me so much

32:46.089 --> 32:48.841
that he gave me an advance
on two years of work,

32:49.342 --> 32:50.343
a hundred million won.

32:54.180 --> 32:55.974
- Are you serious?
- Yeah.

32:56.057 --> 33:00.353
We can use this money
to pay off our debt right away, you know?

33:01.437 --> 33:02.480
Oh…

33:05.650 --> 33:06.526
Mm-hm.

33:09.028 --> 33:11.572
I feel like I've destroyed your dreams.

33:12.073 --> 33:14.534
No, Mom, that's not true.

33:16.244 --> 33:18.496
Us having a home
matters more than anything to me, okay?

33:19.706 --> 33:21.332
I can keep training hard
while I'm working,

33:21.416 --> 33:24.252
and then I can start boxing again
when the pandemic is over.

33:26.963 --> 33:28.506
Sorry for all of this.

33:29.507 --> 33:30.341
Hey, Mom.

33:32.176 --> 33:34.971
You… You should be happy, Mom.

33:35.471 --> 33:37.098
Smile. This is good news.

33:39.017 --> 33:39.851
Yeah.

33:45.314 --> 33:46.482
Thanks, bro.

34:08.546 --> 34:10.590
- Evening, sir.
- Out of the way. Come on.

34:13.009 --> 34:13.843
What?

34:14.635 --> 34:16.054
Your guest has been waiting.

34:16.137 --> 34:16.971
He's early.

34:17.055 --> 34:19.223
That's Iil Group's eldest.

34:19.307 --> 34:22.769
- Yeah, so?
- Love, just be careful.

34:23.352 --> 34:24.228
- Why?
- Over here!

34:24.312 --> 34:25.480
Yes, sir.

34:26.856 --> 34:28.107
Can you get me some wet wipes?

34:28.191 --> 34:31.027
I pressed the button a bunch of times,
but no one came.

34:31.110 --> 34:32.612
I'm sorry. I'll get some now.

34:32.695 --> 34:34.739
Back when I used to work at Speed,

34:34.822 --> 34:36.699
that guy got drunk
and picked a fight with the owner.

34:36.783 --> 34:39.035
- Hyeon-ji?
- Yeah, her.

34:39.118 --> 34:41.704
They had an argument
talking about politics

34:41.788 --> 34:45.208
then days later,
the store was suddenly audited.

34:45.833 --> 34:48.044
She sold her house to pay the taxes.

34:48.836 --> 34:52.131
We found out later
his family is super connected.

34:52.215 --> 34:54.717
National Tax Service, the police force…

34:55.468 --> 34:56.803
They really know everyone.

34:56.886 --> 34:58.429
Well, chaebols are like that.

34:59.263 --> 35:00.139
Oh, yeah?

35:00.640 --> 35:03.101
I guess
they probably insulted a family member.

35:03.184 --> 35:04.435
Ah.

35:05.686 --> 35:07.772
It's just I'm worried about you, honey.

35:09.273 --> 35:10.191
Thank you.

35:10.942 --> 35:12.568
You arranged for pretty some girls, right?

35:13.611 --> 35:14.987
No, he told me not to.

35:18.032 --> 35:20.159
I see. Don't worry, okay?

35:22.036 --> 35:23.329
He brought someone.

35:23.412 --> 35:25.123
- Who?
- He's an officer.

35:28.793 --> 35:29.961
Really?

35:30.044 --> 35:32.213
Yeah, graduated top of his class.

35:35.508 --> 35:36.384
Know him?

35:37.969 --> 35:39.929
I only know him by reputation, sir.

35:46.644 --> 35:48.521
Make sure to keep it cool in there.

35:49.021 --> 35:51.149
- Understood?
- Yeah.

35:55.278 --> 35:56.904
- I'll put in a call.
- Yeah.

35:59.699 --> 36:00.700
No need for that.

36:00.783 --> 36:02.034
- Gentlemen.
- Hm.

36:02.743 --> 36:03.703
About time.

36:04.704 --> 36:07.582
This here is my dear cousin.

36:07.665 --> 36:09.625
I'm Min Gang-yong. Nice to meet you.

36:09.709 --> 36:11.335
You have a great voice.

36:11.419 --> 36:12.628
Kim Myeong-gil.

36:12.712 --> 36:14.797
I hope you don't mind that I tagged along

36:14.881 --> 36:16.465
for a couple of drinks.

36:16.549 --> 36:19.969
I hear that you're a very important man.
It's an honor to meet you, sir.

36:20.052 --> 36:21.137
It's all mine.

36:22.180 --> 36:24.765
This is Lee Jin-su.
He's an associate of mine.

36:24.849 --> 36:26.142
Oh.

36:26.225 --> 36:28.644
Hold on, have we met before by any chance?

36:28.728 --> 36:30.563
No, I just have one of those faces.

36:30.646 --> 36:32.064
I'm sorry.

36:32.648 --> 36:34.942
- Have a seat.
- Sure.

36:37.945 --> 36:40.573
I didn't feel comfortable
drinking on your dime.

36:41.199 --> 36:43.367
It was my intention to offer.

36:46.537 --> 36:47.413
Please, let me.

36:52.835 --> 36:55.087
I'm sorry.
Unfortunately, he doesn't drink.

36:55.171 --> 36:58.216
Ah, you can't be
the only sober person here.

36:58.299 --> 37:02.637
Getting drunk together means
no one can change their minds later on.

37:02.720 --> 37:05.431
Then be a good friend and drink his share.

37:05.514 --> 37:07.266
You seem like a pretty strong drinker.

37:07.350 --> 37:08.726
Loyalty.

37:10.311 --> 37:11.604
Please go ahead and pour it.

37:25.618 --> 37:27.119
Like a real expert.

37:27.828 --> 37:28.871
Smooth, right?

37:29.580 --> 37:30.456
Yeah.

37:30.957 --> 37:32.458
Let me pour you one now.

37:33.876 --> 37:35.044
Would you like a shot as well?

37:35.920 --> 37:38.130
I had a bigger glass in mind.

37:38.214 --> 37:40.049
- Top me off, sir.
- Here.

37:44.053 --> 37:47.306
I'm just a lowly government employee
used to drinking soju bombs,

37:47.390 --> 37:51.269
but tonight, I drink blue.

37:57.275 --> 37:58.526
Now let me.

38:26.971 --> 38:28.514
Hell of a drinker.

38:29.098 --> 38:30.266
I'll have a glass.

38:30.933 --> 38:31.892
It's my liquor.

38:32.893 --> 38:33.728
Hm?

38:34.937 --> 38:35.938
Let me pour it for you.

38:41.235 --> 38:42.153
Please.

38:56.709 --> 38:57.793
And you.

39:04.759 --> 39:05.843
Oh, yeah.

39:06.427 --> 39:07.887
Cheers!

39:09.472 --> 39:10.306
Cheers.

39:24.820 --> 39:26.655
You both drink very well.

39:27.448 --> 39:30.326
Cousin, if I get drunk and offensive,
stop me.

39:30.409 --> 39:32.036
If that happens…

39:32.119 --> 39:34.372
Where is it? I'll…

39:38.292 --> 39:39.251
arrest you.

39:45.883 --> 39:47.218
Let's drink more. Come on.

40:04.819 --> 40:05.778
Oh, fuck me.

40:07.154 --> 40:09.615
Now that we've shared
some drinks together,

40:10.908 --> 40:12.159
let's be frank here.

40:13.160 --> 40:14.078
Let's do it.

40:15.871 --> 40:16.789
Are you rich?

40:16.872 --> 40:19.458
I've worked hard my whole life
to make my money.

40:21.168 --> 40:22.253
How much?

40:23.462 --> 40:24.338
It's enough.

40:25.089 --> 40:26.632
And all of it is legitimate.

40:26.715 --> 40:28.300
Is that so?

40:29.844 --> 40:31.262
That's odd.

40:31.345 --> 40:34.849
I heard
if you looked at Smile Capital's assets,

40:35.349 --> 40:36.976
you'd barely find 50 billion.

40:37.059 --> 40:38.602
You're right.

40:38.686 --> 40:41.397
I wonder
if the National Tax Agency knows that.

40:41.480 --> 40:42.857
Should we call them?

40:43.732 --> 40:45.192
Oh no, you're drunk.

40:45.276 --> 40:47.987
Look how much you've upset Mr. Kim.
Apologize to him.

40:48.612 --> 40:49.697
Oh, I'm sorry.

40:50.448 --> 40:52.283
I've been drinking on an empty stomach.

40:53.451 --> 40:54.827
It's hitting me hard.

40:55.411 --> 40:57.580
Don't you worry.
We have all the money you need.

40:59.165 --> 41:00.249
Oh, yeah?

41:01.292 --> 41:02.126
Okay.

41:02.918 --> 41:05.671
I guess I should never worry about money.

41:08.257 --> 41:12.178
Oh, yeah. My mom sends her regards
to Chairman Bang.

41:13.179 --> 41:15.514
She is very thankful.

41:16.140 --> 41:18.642
But the man
who got her the money that day…

41:22.271 --> 41:24.398
was apparently in his mid-40s.

41:25.524 --> 41:29.612
How do you manage to look so good
after 20 years?

41:30.738 --> 41:32.031
Is it plastic surgery?

41:33.199 --> 41:35.159
A face lift!

41:37.703 --> 41:38.621
I see.

41:38.704 --> 41:41.790
You thought
I wouldn't ask my own mother, huh?

41:41.874 --> 41:43.292
Come on, out with it!

41:43.375 --> 41:44.919
Why so quiet?

41:45.544 --> 41:49.590
Huh? You're just not gonna talk now?

41:52.635 --> 41:54.720
Did they teach you not talk in prison?

41:56.805 --> 41:59.683
This guy's laughing.

41:59.767 --> 42:01.977
Sure, smile all you want.

42:03.521 --> 42:05.689
God damn! Well,

42:06.398 --> 42:08.692
I'm done drinking. Let's wrap it up.

42:10.611 --> 42:11.654
Mr. Kim.

42:12.488 --> 42:14.031
I won't make the call.

42:14.782 --> 42:17.076
As long as we never cross paths again.

42:19.119 --> 42:20.204
Kimmie.

42:22.498 --> 42:23.374
Come on now.

42:34.635 --> 42:35.719
If you ever

42:36.303 --> 42:38.389
mess with my family again,

42:40.224 --> 42:41.433
you'll die.

42:47.606 --> 42:48.482
You understand?

42:49.358 --> 42:50.818
Hm?

42:52.403 --> 42:56.240
Oh man,
look at this scary knife wound here. Whoa!

42:56.907 --> 42:59.034
- He's the real deal.
- Let's go.

42:59.118 --> 43:01.495
You're right. We've been here too long.

43:01.579 --> 43:04.415
I tried to give you
the benefit of the doubt.

43:04.498 --> 43:06.834
I thought you were a hard-working man.

43:19.346 --> 43:20.180
Jang-do.

43:20.681 --> 43:21.515
Yeah?

43:22.933 --> 43:25.769
You'll follow Beom.
Find something we can use.

43:26.520 --> 43:27.688
Something big.

43:29.732 --> 43:30.566
I'm on it, sir.

43:31.066 --> 43:33.986
ANTIQUES SHOPPING CENTER

43:40.909 --> 43:43.662
- Hey, thanks for coming with me.
- Oh, no problem.

43:46.915 --> 43:48.083
Wait.

43:48.584 --> 43:49.501
What?

43:49.585 --> 43:51.837
- Uh, are you coming in?
- Yeah.

43:51.920 --> 43:55.007
I'm gonna make my case to Mr. Choi
and get a job as well.

43:55.090 --> 43:56.008
We could work together.

43:56.091 --> 43:57.801
That would be awesome.

43:57.885 --> 44:00.012
Right?! So talk me up, add some flavor.

44:00.095 --> 44:01.513
MSG.

44:01.597 --> 44:03.349
- Mm-hm.
- Cool. Let's go.

44:25.746 --> 44:27.414
- Morning!
- Hello!

44:30.000 --> 44:31.168
I see you found your way here.

44:31.251 --> 44:32.503
Yes.

44:32.586 --> 44:33.420
And this morning,

44:33.504 --> 44:35.964
I used the advance you gave me
to pay off my family's loans.

44:36.048 --> 44:38.092
Thank you so much.
Really, thank you so much.

44:41.136 --> 44:42.846
I have faith that you'll do very well.

44:42.930 --> 44:44.807
I'll give it everything I have.

44:44.890 --> 44:47.810
Good morning, sir! I'm Hong Woo-jin.

44:47.893 --> 44:50.938
I've helped Mr. Moon with his work
in the past.

44:51.438 --> 44:54.817
I'm a close friend of Gun-woo's
from our time in the Marines.

44:54.900 --> 44:56.068
Yeah.

44:56.151 --> 44:58.362
Watching his struggles
from the sidelines,

44:59.113 --> 45:01.699
I was truly ashamed
that I couldn't help him more

45:01.782 --> 45:03.367
because of my very limited means.

45:03.450 --> 45:04.284
It killed me inside.

45:05.119 --> 45:07.746
I'm relieved he met someone like you
who could help him out.

45:08.455 --> 45:10.165
I'm really grateful that happened.

45:10.249 --> 45:13.627
I also believe that I, Hong Woo-jin,
may also be of service to you.

45:14.420 --> 45:16.338
I've done this kind of work before.

45:17.965 --> 45:20.759
Not to toot my own horn too much
in front of you,

45:20.843 --> 45:22.553
but I was thinking maybe it would…

45:23.804 --> 45:25.514
You know, since I know the ropes,

45:26.014 --> 45:29.643
maybe it would be good
since he's just now starting out

45:30.310 --> 45:31.186
for me to help.

45:32.062 --> 45:34.398
Seems like
this would help him adjust quickly.

45:34.481 --> 45:36.692
- And ultimately be in your favor.
- Yeah.

45:37.276 --> 45:39.319
And with these thoughts in mind,
that led me to you.

45:39.903 --> 45:41.155
With your permission,

45:41.238 --> 45:43.365
I'd like to help Gun-woo
with his work, sir!

45:50.914 --> 45:51.832
Sure, why not?

45:55.586 --> 45:56.503
Thank you.

45:57.880 --> 45:58.839
Sit down.

45:58.922 --> 45:59.840
- Sir.
- Sir.

46:02.384 --> 46:04.553
- Thank you, sir!
- Thanks so much.

46:05.053 --> 46:07.473
There is one thing I didn't mention
when we first met.

46:07.556 --> 46:08.515
Oh.

46:08.599 --> 46:11.769
I may be the one paying you,
but I'm not gonna be the one hiring you.

46:12.478 --> 46:13.312
Sorry?

46:13.395 --> 46:15.606
You still have to interview with Hyeon-ju.

46:17.858 --> 46:23.071
Ah, uh, so what would happen
if I were to fail the interview, sir?

46:23.155 --> 46:25.115
You'd have to return
all the money I gave you.

46:25.741 --> 46:30.287
Oh, but already I used all of it
to pay back our loan.

46:30.370 --> 46:32.122
I believe you'll do very well with her.

46:32.790 --> 46:33.624
Huh?

46:34.708 --> 46:39.505
Although she's not very keen on the idea
of having a bodyguard around.

46:39.588 --> 46:42.257
But you know I'm terrible with words,
Mr. Choi.

46:42.758 --> 46:44.301
Good luck.

46:44.384 --> 46:46.470
Um, sir.

46:46.553 --> 46:49.848
If I can convince her
to hire both me and Gun-woo,

46:49.932 --> 46:52.518
sir, would that mean
I also get to receive a salary?

46:55.395 --> 46:56.688
Okay.

46:56.772 --> 46:57.689
Nice.

46:59.316 --> 47:01.527
All right,
I have a scalp massage I have to get to.

47:01.610 --> 47:02.903
- Oh, yes.
- Yeah.

47:02.986 --> 47:04.613
Sir, please enjoy your time.

47:04.696 --> 47:05.697
Also…

47:07.658 --> 47:11.370
Use this… to get yourself some food.

47:11.453 --> 47:12.287
Uh…

47:13.163 --> 47:15.374
Uh, thank you, sir.

47:16.917 --> 47:19.294
You really know how to take care
of your employees.

47:22.548 --> 47:23.882
You two…

47:26.552 --> 47:28.428
should stick together no matter what.

47:29.805 --> 47:30.639
Oh.

47:30.722 --> 47:31.640
- Yes!
- Yes!

47:32.140 --> 47:33.058
Godspeed!

47:33.141 --> 47:34.184
- Godspeed!
- Godspeed!

47:45.821 --> 47:46.780
Wait a minute.

47:55.038 --> 47:55.873
Shit, bro.

47:57.165 --> 47:58.166
- What?
- Look!

47:58.250 --> 47:59.376
What happened?

48:00.252 --> 48:02.337
- It was in here.
- Really?

48:02.838 --> 48:05.173
That's… That's gotta be millions.

48:05.257 --> 48:06.508
No. Wait.

48:12.264 --> 48:13.140
Whoa.

48:14.975 --> 48:16.560
Oh God, there's even more.

48:18.228 --> 48:19.146
No way.

48:38.457 --> 48:41.710
THERE WILL BE GUESTS AT THE BOOKSTORE
HAVE A NICE CHAT

48:42.502 --> 48:43.587
Oh shit.

48:44.588 --> 48:48.425
17 billion, 18 billion,

48:48.508 --> 48:51.178
19…

48:52.220 --> 48:53.347
21…

48:54.056 --> 48:55.599
- Uh…
- 22.

48:56.391 --> 48:58.518
I think I've met Hyeon-ju before.

48:59.311 --> 49:01.521
Huh? You've met?

49:02.189 --> 49:04.358
When I went over to see you
a few days ago,

49:05.108 --> 49:07.736
she was, uh, chasing a homeless person,

49:07.819 --> 49:11.073
so I stepped in,
and then Hyeon-ju tased me.

49:11.156 --> 49:13.325
- You got tased?
- Mm-hm.

49:13.909 --> 49:15.619
And then what? Did you two fight?

49:15.702 --> 49:19.206
Nuh-uh. She just cussed me out and left.

49:19.289 --> 49:20.791
Oh…

49:23.126 --> 49:24.127
You got me.

49:24.711 --> 49:26.338
I'll be sure to take care of it.

49:26.421 --> 49:27.839
You just keep, yeah.

49:28.507 --> 49:30.842
- Mm.
- Just keep… keep your head down.

49:32.177 --> 49:33.637
You made me lose count.

49:33.720 --> 49:34.596
My bad.

49:42.312 --> 49:43.146
Oh!

49:44.940 --> 49:46.191
Hello, Ms. Hyeon-ju.

49:46.274 --> 49:47.275
How are you?

49:47.359 --> 49:51.405
We were both hand-picked by Mr. Choi,
so you can safely go about your work.

49:52.698 --> 49:56.785
#GoOn. #SecurityGuard.

49:56.868 --> 49:58.120
#Manager.

49:58.203 --> 50:02.416
#Brother. Brother.

50:02.958 --> 50:04.543
What was that?

50:04.626 --> 50:05.460
Brother.

50:05.544 --> 50:07.754
Welcome your two new best friends.

50:10.841 --> 50:14.302
Um, uh, say the word,
and we'll…

50:14.886 --> 50:17.055
- Anything you need.
- I don't need anything.

50:19.599 --> 50:22.227
Uh yeah, um, but we'll…

50:22.310 --> 50:24.104
…whenever you decide
to call on us to do it.

50:24.187 --> 50:27.149
Oh, no, I won't need anything ever,
so leave.

50:31.028 --> 50:32.112
- Mm.
- Mm.

50:33.196 --> 50:34.614
You don't like us?

50:35.240 --> 50:37.075
How would I know when we've just me?

50:37.701 --> 50:38.618
I don't need you.

50:38.702 --> 50:41.872
You haven't seen us work yet,
so how would you know?

50:42.539 --> 50:45.709
I haven't had a problem doing everything
completely on my own so far.

50:45.792 --> 50:47.169
That's how I know.

50:47.836 --> 50:49.463
I hate people that argue.

50:49.546 --> 50:50.797
I'm not arguing.

50:50.881 --> 50:51.882
You just did it again.

50:53.717 --> 50:54.634
Get out.

51:01.224 --> 51:04.227
Mr. Choi told us
this was the arrangement, okay?

51:05.187 --> 51:06.813
Not that you had to persuade me?

51:09.149 --> 51:11.401
So now you're lying to me?

51:12.819 --> 51:14.529
I only thought your shoes were fake.

51:15.530 --> 51:16.364
Leave.

51:18.033 --> 51:19.326
It's time to go!

51:20.911 --> 51:21.995
Hello?

51:22.079 --> 51:23.038
What are you? Deaf?

51:23.538 --> 51:25.832
Hit the road. Go!

51:45.143 --> 51:47.771
I really, really need this job.

51:47.854 --> 51:49.564
Please just let me work here for a month.

51:49.648 --> 51:51.483
If I'm no help, I'll leave.

51:51.566 --> 51:53.819
I promise. Just give me a month.
Please, I'm begging you.

51:54.319 --> 51:55.278
Listen,

51:55.362 --> 51:58.115
if you need to borrow money,
my grandpa will lend you some.

51:59.157 --> 52:00.826
I'll be sure to put in a good word
for you.

52:01.660 --> 52:02.869
This is awkward.

52:02.953 --> 52:03.787
But he already…

52:05.789 --> 52:10.752
He already gave me a two-year advancement
on the pay because…

52:10.836 --> 52:13.338
…there's a Smile Capital loan
that my mom took out.

52:14.840 --> 52:16.424
And they completely duped her.

52:17.342 --> 52:20.512
I had to pay it
with all the money he gave me.

52:20.595 --> 52:25.058
If… If I have to pay that money,
then we lose our house.

52:25.559 --> 52:28.478
So please, just help me this one time.

52:31.690 --> 52:32.566
Get up now.

52:33.400 --> 52:34.317
You hungry?

52:44.578 --> 52:46.705
Smile Capital loaned you money?

52:47.622 --> 52:49.374
They conned my mom.

52:50.667 --> 52:52.335
How big was the loan then?

52:53.461 --> 52:54.713
A hundred mill.

52:55.505 --> 52:59.134
And you paid it off with no penalties?

52:59.968 --> 53:01.928
They destroyed my mom's café.

53:02.512 --> 53:04.806
It's a total mess now.

53:07.976 --> 53:10.687
They did that to your face?

53:12.147 --> 53:13.023
Yeah.

53:15.442 --> 53:16.776
I'm sure you're pissed.

53:18.403 --> 53:19.821
Did you go to the police?

53:20.864 --> 53:21.698
No way.

53:24.367 --> 53:26.536
They threatened to kill my mother
if I called the police.

53:27.829 --> 53:28.663
Who did?

53:30.290 --> 53:31.499
It was their boss.

53:31.583 --> 53:35.128
Delicious hamburgers have arrived. Here.

53:37.672 --> 53:38.798
Listen, then eat.

53:45.388 --> 53:46.640
Maybe you've heard

53:46.723 --> 53:48.892
my grandpa gives out zero-interest loans

53:48.975 --> 53:51.394
to people who are down on their luck
and really need them.

53:51.978 --> 53:55.482
But some people try to take advantage
of his generosity.

53:56.858 --> 53:58.610
Yang Jae-myeong is one.

53:59.611 --> 54:02.155
He borrowed ten million for his mom,

54:02.239 --> 54:03.740
then he just disappeared.

54:04.241 --> 54:05.992
Took me half a year to find him.

54:07.327 --> 54:09.663
Begging at a train station.

54:10.997 --> 54:14.209
I thought Yang Jae-myeong
had really become homeless,

54:14.292 --> 54:18.588
then I saw his pearly whites.

54:19.547 --> 54:21.049
So I decided to tail him.

54:21.675 --> 54:25.720
I found out that he and his goons
were pretending to be homeless

54:25.804 --> 54:28.473
and stealing IDs
from the actual homeless at night.

54:29.307 --> 54:31.559
They use them to start shell corporations.

54:32.894 --> 54:37.816
Then con the loan sharks
taking thousands, sometimes millions.

54:39.651 --> 54:41.528
It all looks very professional,

54:41.611 --> 54:43.863
so someone has to be pulling the strings
behind the scenes.

54:45.907 --> 54:49.369
This guy was seen speaking
with Yang Jae-myeong.

54:50.662 --> 54:51.496
Know him?

54:56.167 --> 54:57.294
I do.

55:02.674 --> 55:04.759
Our goal tonight is to get an exact count

55:04.843 --> 55:08.096
on how many IDs
these thugs are stealing each day.

55:08.179 --> 55:10.390
Stay calm no matter what.

55:10.473 --> 55:11.850
If they know we're onto them,

55:11.933 --> 55:13.601
then all my work has been for nothing.

55:17.856 --> 55:19.733
IDENTIFICATION CARD

56:30.970 --> 56:32.931
Cover your faces and hang back.

56:59.290 --> 57:00.792
Hey. How about this guy?

57:01.543 --> 57:02.669
He's piss-drunk.

57:02.752 --> 57:04.379
He might have something on him.

57:06.506 --> 57:07.465
Go, go.

57:10.802 --> 57:12.345
Look, there, there.

57:12.429 --> 57:14.055
Find someone who isn't wasted.

57:14.139 --> 57:15.140
Okay.

57:17.100 --> 57:18.435
- Come on.
- Okay.

57:18.518 --> 57:20.186
- Hey, let's go.
- Okay.

57:41.207 --> 57:42.459
Head down.

57:51.134 --> 57:52.135
Hello, sir.

57:52.844 --> 57:54.846
Uh, what? Huh?

57:54.929 --> 57:58.475
You shouldn't be sleeping
on this cold floor with flimsy newspaper.

57:58.558 --> 58:00.894
You should put something else down first.

58:00.977 --> 58:02.061
Yeah.

58:02.687 --> 58:05.106
Have you eaten yet?

58:05.190 --> 58:07.442
Uh, two days ago.

58:07.525 --> 58:09.736
Ah. We're here to help you.

58:09.819 --> 58:12.489
We're here with a homeless charity
funded by the city.

58:13.281 --> 58:14.491
Oh, I see.

58:14.574 --> 58:18.495
The government created this organization
so we could help each other out, okay?

58:18.578 --> 58:19.537
You can join us.

58:21.080 --> 58:23.750
If you join,
you won't have to sit out here like this.

58:24.375 --> 58:25.627
We'll find you a job.

58:26.419 --> 58:29.214
Every single month,
we'll give you 20 free masks.

58:29.881 --> 58:33.510
And you'll get a monthly stipend,
300,000 won.

58:34.010 --> 58:35.803
- Three hundred?
- Yeah.

58:36.721 --> 58:38.056
- Sir.
- Yeah?

58:38.139 --> 58:41.601
Listen, if you have an ID with you,
we can just do the registration right now.

58:41.684 --> 58:43.770
You'll have the money in a month.
Sound good?

58:44.687 --> 58:45.772
What do you say, huh?

58:45.855 --> 58:47.106
- Yeah.
- Great.

58:49.275 --> 58:50.193
Here.

58:52.028 --> 58:54.739
Not everyone can participate.
Keep it quiet, okay?

58:55.615 --> 58:56.449
Thanks.

58:56.533 --> 58:58.409
Damn, that guy's got a silver tongue.

58:58.493 --> 58:59.410
Thank you.

59:02.497 --> 59:03.915
Four IDs so far…

59:15.802 --> 59:17.887
- Excuse me, sir.
- What?

59:18.888 --> 59:21.099
We're here with the Homeless Association
to help people.

59:21.182 --> 59:22.559
- What the--
- Yeah.

59:22.642 --> 59:24.143
It's you again!

59:24.644 --> 59:27.438
You son of a bitch.
Where's my ID? Give it back!

59:27.522 --> 59:31.234
You crazy…
You crazy old bastard. Fucker!

59:32.402 --> 59:33.778
Let me go, you old fuck!

59:35.780 --> 59:37.365
Old ass piece of shit!

59:37.448 --> 59:39.742
No, we can't help.
